# This is the single executable POSIX /bin/sh implementation of safe-rm.
# Specialized from the selfmanaged Type 0 ship unit (direction A → B only).
# Inherited: self-install, version-check, self-update, self-uninstall, about, out_*.
# Domain: rm with a path guard and --dry-run (requirement-domain-safe-rm.md).
# Project requirements (docs/requirements/ only — never cite templates here):
# - requirement-shell-cli-interface.md
# - requirement-shell-cli-self-install.md    (self-install; $0 copy vs download; dest 0755/0700)
# - requirement-shell-cli-zero-arguments.md  (Type O empty argv = install-ensure)
# - requirement-shell-cli-storage.md         (util_resolve_storage + about fields)
# - requirement-shell-idempotency.md
# - requirement-shell-self-management.md
# - requirement-shell-modular-function-design.md
# - requirement-shell-output-requirements.md
# - requirement-shell-interactive-vs-noninteractive.md
# - requirement-shell-automatic-checksum.md
# - requirement-domain-safe-rm.md          (rm guard, --dry-run, refuse classes)
# Plus CIAO Protection Zones and "DO NOT MODIFY" rules.
#
# Philosophy: CIAO (Caution • Intentional • Anti-fragile • Over-engineered)
# Single file for curl | sh compatibility.
#
# APP NAME: hard-assign APP_NAME="safe-rm" (extractor parity with VERSION); optional := default after.
# REPO_USER / REPO_NAME: GitHub owner/repo identity for the install channel.
# SCRIPT_RELPATH: path of this file inside the repository (default src/${APP_NAME}).
# SCRIPT_URL: product channel SSOT — composed from repo identity + SCRIPT_RELPATH (raw content URL).
